  "period_note": "HALF-YEARLY filing (occupies the Q2 slot per project convention). Balance sheet is the 30-Jun-2022 period-end snapshot (reported), Solo basis. Income statement items are CUMULATIVE from 1 January 2022 (H1=6 months). OCR'd (pdftoppm 300dpi + tesseract). Comparative (31-Dec-2021) column matches this dataset's existing 2021_Q4.json exactly for total_assets (310,366.413296m), total_equity (17,473.661601m), paid_up_capital (9,340.40456m), statutory_reserve (6,721.41491m), total_deposits (231,122.860626m) and off_balance_sheet_exposures (65,075.728293m). Balance-sheet identity holds exactly (302,324.995865 + 18,094.121867 = 320,419.117732). statutory_reserve corroborated by the 20%-of-PBT rule (6,721.41491m + 20% x 1,287.553968m = 6,978.925704m, matches 6,978.925703m reported to rounding). Income statement fully reconciles: operating_profit = total_operating_income - total_operating_expenses (4,907.454345-2,722.195582=2,185.258763, matches 2,185.258762m reported); profit_before_tax = operating_profit - total_provision (2,185.258762-897.704795=1,287.553967, matches 1,287.553968m reported); profit_after_tax = profit_before_tax - tax_expense (1,287.553968-421.587604=865.966364 exact). Current tax (470.927751m) exceeds the total tax subtotal (421.587604m), implying a net deferred-tax CREDIT of -49.340147m this half-year - consistent with the small deferred-tax credits also seen in Q1-2022 (-17.566625m, per the cross-referenced figure) and 9M-2022 (-28.505761m, see 2022_Q3.json), i.e. a persistent pattern of modest deferred-tax credits partly offsetting a rising current-tax charge through 2022. eps_cumulative was illegible for the current period; CALCULATED as profit_after_tax / weighted-average shares = 865.966364m / 934.040456m shares = 0.93 (consistent with a visible '993' OCR fragment).",
